message: "If you use this repository in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Structural Theory of AI Reasoning — From LLM Unfolding to Structural Localization and Living Reasoning"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Tan"
    given-names: "Sizhe"

abstract: >-
  Structural Theory of AI Reasoning develops a structural explanation of AI reasoning
  that connects the latent and distributed reasoning capabilities of Large Language
  Models with the explicit localization, traversal, gap bridging, forward extension,
  validation, persistence, and structural growth mechanisms of Structural Intelligence.
  The repository distinguishes reasoning answers from reasoning structure growth,
  interprets LLM reasoning through a Folding–Unfolding framework, introduces the
  complementary relation between LLM Unfolding and Structural Intelligence Localization,
  and develops a Living Reasoning Loop in which validated reasoning outputs can become
  persistent infrastructure for future reasoning. It further explores future reasoning
  architectures based on heterogeneous Per-Node intelligence, Calling Graphs, TaskGraphs,
  Action Calling Graphs, Structural Runtimes, Runtime Invariants, specialized Unfolding
  engines, and governed autonomous structural growth.

